  "hints": [
    "Ignore the minimisation for a moment. If somebody handed you a largest allowed piece sum, could you check in one pass whether exactly m pieces are enough?",
    "Feasibility is monotone: if a limit works, every larger limit works too. Binary search the limit between the largest single element and the total of the array.",
    "For a fixed limit, pack greedily: keep adding elements while the running sum stays within the limit, otherwise close the piece and open a new one, then ask whether the piece count is at most m."
